hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-71 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-71 = cons "**Symmetry orbits, global content addressing, and zero-decompression conductance.** For graphs, molecules, codebases, meshes, and versioned corpora (Part I §4.2 `GraphSym`, §8.3 `AdjList`, `pack-equiv`), quotienting by a symmetry group or proved equivalence collapses an entire orbit of distinct byte strings to one canonical representative stored once by content key plus a compact witness path transporting back to each concrete instance. Because the compressed representation is the live interaction net and content-addressed store rather than an opaque archive blob, queries, proofs, incremental edits (`Derivative`, Part I §10.2), and peer exchanges (`peer-transparent`, `lib/pool.cub`) operate directly on the compressed DAG, unfolding locally only as far as read (`memory-is-local`) and deduplicating globally across files, versions, modalities, and peers without materializing a corpus on one machine." (cons "" nil)
